How to fit tests
  We have unknown pools of students taking the 3 tests (xuece, tongce, zhikao)
  We fit a piecewise linear function (or step function if that's easier) to the pdfs of these three functions
  Integrals must match the observed number of students
  Probably we only want 2-3 steps or 2 linear pieces for each test. Optimize to reduce error in the agreement between thresholds where they overlap.
  Test outcomes are percentiles in the test taker pool. All we want is to convert these to percentiles in the original pool. There is no need for any other fancy distortion or correlation.
